== 7. Findings of the first pre-check round (10 Nov, 20:40-21:35 UTC), all on the test side, fixed before delivery
The first round ran the same RTL as above. Its failures, and what changed:
1. TL01's coverage bins 'local bursts in region r' were empty at 5 of 13 seeds on 4x4 with 2x2 regions (seed 1 with
   +QUICK; seeds 2, 3, 5, 6 and 8), at seeds 2-3 with SAFE, B_MAX 15, 2 VCs and XY routing, and at seed 1 with B_MAX 15
   and 2 VCs. The bins counted only part b, the region traffic, whose packets rarely travel by bypass (0.1-0.8% of
   packets here: the open question of B5, for E0). Fix (tests_two.svh): the bins count from the start of part a,
   whose held packets give every region one local burst by design; part b adds those it happens to make.
2. With B_MAX 5, TL02 failed at every seed: 'cycle 1374: 1 NIs where bypass writes and the NI lookahead disagree;
   first R15, write 1, announced cycles 1377..1381', then all 16 NIs in cycles 1379-1381. mesh_checker kept one
   announced window per NI. With B_MAX 5 a 2x2 region's subslot is 5 cycles, so 5-flit bursts reach an NI in
   consecutive subslots, and its next lookahead (3 cycles before the first write) came while the last burst was
   still being written, replacing that burst's window. Fix (mesh_checker.sv): one bit per announced cycle for every
   link and NI, shifted every cycle, so any number of bursts can be announced; an announcement that overlaps one
   already made is still a collision.
3. With B_MAX 5, TL04 failed at seeds 2 and 3: 'at the end of the slot before cycle 8551, 10 flits stay reserved, 2
   reservations wait for a lookahead (model)'. TL04 required no open reservation in a slot's last cycle. With B_MAX 5
   and TIGHT subslots T = 2*Hmax + 1, so the lookahead of the last subslot's longest path is due exactly in the
   slot's last cycle, and its reservation is open in that cycle (released at its end), in the RTL and the model
   alike. Fix (tests_two.svh): no reservation may be due after its slot ends (ni_checker's due cycles), and the RTL
   may hold B_MAX flits for each open reservation and nothing else.
4. Design A's benches (tb_mesh, tb_mesh_dl) did not build: -Wall found plan_req unused, since only design C's
   checker block reads it. Fix (mesh_bench.sv): a lint waiver on its declaration.
No check count at seed 1 changed (a coverage bin counts as one check either way, and the masks check the same
cycles). After the fixes every TL test passes at 13 seeds on 4x4 and with B_MAX 5, the other configurations at
seeds 1-3, and design A builds clean with B5's counts. The RTL did not change between the rounds.

== Review (by hand, 11 Nov)
- RTL changed in B6: sched_pkg (frame numbers, k_L), phase_sequencer (new), resv_ctrl and ni (local gaps, dec_loc),
  tile (the second timetable under the sequencer, the plan input), mesh_top (REGION_N, K_FIXED, EPOCH, plan_i).
  Designs A and B: tile and mesh_top tie dec_loc to 0 and ignore the plan, so their behaviour is B5's: every U, R,
  N and BP count above equals B5's. Yosys gives design A's tile B5's 44,882 cells exactly; design B's 63,775 against
  B5's 63,761 (+0.02%, ABC mapping a slightly different netlist of the same logic).
- D50: with REGION_N = MESH_N the sequencer keeps one counter (g_one), checked against design B on every link and
  cycle by TL05 on 4x4. D52: the sample in an epoch's cycle 255 and the frame-start rule are checked by U11 (every
  cycle against frame_ref, a sample in a frame's last cycle included) and by TL03-TL04 in the mesh.
- Section 0's five calls in loop conditions are the ones reviewed since B1-B2 (queues and states read in the
  condition, no function with loops of its own); none is in a B6 file.
- Mutation check (B6_mutation.log): the first run killed 22 of 24. S10 is equivalent; P02, an epoch sized at
  k_L = 3, gave the same power of two as k_L = 4 in every configuration U11 checked. U11 gained a thirteenth
  package check (the epoch on 8x8 with B_MAX 5: 2^15, where k_L = 3 would give 2^14), which moved U11's counts
  by one (21,000,066 to 21,000,067; +QUICK 2,625,052 to 2,625,053), and a mutant S13 was added. The final run
  kills all 24 non-equivalent mutants, every one by the testbench alone.
- The 16x16 functional run cannot be made here (memory); it is the one exit check left to xsim alone.
